\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The audited setting and the three gated questions. \textbf  {(a)}~A teacher prefills a long context $x$ and stores its cache $C_T(x)$; a translator maps that stored cache into the student's cache space, and the student answers a short query $q$ from the translated cache $\hat  {C}_S(x)$. The red crossed path is the strict zero-re-prefill constraint: no context token enters the student's forward pass. The audit scores the handoff by the change in gold-letter probability against the student's own prefill (baseline), with the teacher's full prefill as the capability upper bound. \textbf  {(b)}~The three questions can fail independently (Section~\ref {sec:intro}), so each carries its own instrument and gate; $\dagger $ marks gates fixed before the runs, and $\ddagger $ marks families and axes added while revising and evaluated under the same gates (Section~\ref {sec:tiers}).}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:framework}{{1}{3}{The audited setting and the three gated questions. \textbf {(a)}~A teacher prefills a long context $x$ and stores its cache $C_T(x)$; a translator maps that stored cache into the student's cache space, and the student answers a short query $q$ from the translated cache $\hat {C}_S(x)$. The red crossed path is the strict zero-re-prefill constraint: no context token enters the student's forward pass. The audit scores the handoff by the change in gold-letter probability against the student's own prefill (baseline), with the teacher's full prefill as the capability upper bound. \textbf {(b)}~The three questions can fail independently (Section~\ref {sec:intro}), so each carries its own instrument and gate; $\dagger $ marks gates fixed before the runs, and $\ddagger $ marks families and axes added while revising and evaluated under the same gates (Section~\ref {sec:tiers})}{figure.1}{}}
